    "id": "p18-q3-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Two coins are tossed. What is the probability of obtaining two heads given that at least one head is obtained?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "worked": "Write H for heads and T for tails, recording the coins in order. The equally likely outcomes are $\\{HH,HT,TH,TT\\}$. Given at least one head, the restricted sample space is $\\{HH,HT,TH\\}$. Only $HH$ gives two heads.\n\n$$P(\\text{two heads}\\mid\\text{at least one head})=\\frac{1}{3}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
